HHANet retains its original PyTorch implementation and model parameter names.

The shifted MLP design is related to UNeXt (Valanarasu and Patel, MICCAI 2022):
https://github.com/jeya-maria-jose/UNeXt-pytorch
The upstream license is preserved in licenses/UNeXt.txt.

Training uses PyTorch, torchvision, Albumentations, OpenCV, NumPy, Pillow,
scikit-learn, and tqdm. These dependencies retain their respective licenses.
